    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d191">

                <pb facs="0191" n="179" xml:id="pg179"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.00/12–3144: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Greece</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacVeagh</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Athens</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-31T14:00:00+02:00">December 31,
                            1944—2 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 31—11:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>205. The establishment of the Regency was announced here this morning and the
                    Archbishop took the oath of office at noon, in the presence of the Holy Synod.
                    As he is himself President of that body and there is no Vice President, the oath
                    was administered by the eldest among the other members. The very brief ceremony
                    was held at the Foreign Office and was attended by the political, military and
                    diplomatic worlds of Athens, despite the fact that invitations were issued only
                    during the forenoon. I saw no insurgents present. Fighting still continues.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">MacVeagh</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
